title: A speech in the Piazza San Sepolcro
subtitle: A new organisation has formed...
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 3 and week = 3
max-visits: 1
tags: event
new-page: true
face-image: img/sepolcro.jpeg

= Formation Of The Fasci

In the hall of Piazza San Sepolcro, a man, that being, Benito Mussolini, speaks to a crowd of atleast 300 people. He speaks of equal suffrage, of direct referendums, of <span style="color: [+ pnf_colour +];">nationalism</span>, of the 8 hour work week, of how the <span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**ali**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**an**</span> people were robbed, given this "mutilated victory" in its wake, as thunderous applause shakes the hall. The FdC has been formed, and has already picked up momentum within the population.

Benito Mussolini was previously a member of our party, the [+ psi_name +], but he was kicked out of it due to his pro-war position  in 1914, due to our party mostly wanting to stay neutral or be openly anti-war.

The party is split on the how we should react to the formation of this new organisation. After all, talks of equal suffrage, of the abolishment of the Senate, of the 8 hour work week.. Do these demands not reflect ours?

- @distrust_watch_closely: Time will only tell what this entails.

@distrust_watch_closely
